s="internal-only" data-internal-only="true">Reader Paths</a><a href="book-universe.html">Book Universe</a><a href="launch-room.html" class="internal-only" data-internal-only="true">Launch Room</a><a href="share-center.html">Share Center</a></div><div class="nav-group"><strong>Evidence & Trust</strong><a href="trust-center.html">Trust Center</a><a href="evidence-vault-index.html">Source Index</a><a href="evidence-policy.html">Evidence Policy</a><a href="black-file.html">Black File</a><a href="download-center.html">Download Center</a><a href="feed-center.html">Feed Center</a></div><div class="nav-group"><strong>Control Maps</strong><a href="power-atlas.html">Power Atlas</a><a href="network-maps.html">Network Maps</a><a href="network-map-index.html">Map Index</a><a href="authority-hub.html">Authority Hub</a><a href="answer-engine.html">AI Answers</a><a href="schema-index.html" class="internal-only" data-internal-only="true">Machine Index</a></div><div class="nav-group"><strong>Freedom Ecosystem</strong><a href="live-intel.html">Live Intel</a><a href="news.html">Intel Desk</a><a href="videos.html">Rumble Channels</a><a href="forum.html">Signal Board</a><a href="timers.html">Timers</a><a href="distribution-center.html" class="internal-only" data-internal-only="true">Distribution</a><a href="update-monitor.html" class="internal-only" data-internal-only="true">Update Monitor</a></div></div></details></nav></header><!-- page-guide:start --><section class="page-guide wrap commercial-internal"><div><span class="label">You are here</span><h2>Evidence route</h2><p>This page is part of the wider reporting system. Start with the summary, then open the evidence route or research tools for deeper source work.</p></div><div class="page-guide-chips"><span>Summary</span><span>Evidence</span><span>Research</span><span>Search</span></div><div class="page-guide-actions"><a class="btn" href="daily-command-brief.html">Today</a><a class="btn alt" href="evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a class="btn alt" href="research-tools.html">Research Tools</a></div></section><!-- page-guide:end --><!-- reader-governor:start --><section class="reader-governor-strip"><div><strong>Matrix Reprogrammed</strong><span>Reports, records, people, institutions, money routes and missing files.</span></div><nav><a href="daily-command-brief.html">Daily Brief</a><a href="control-structure.html">Power Map</a><a href="entities.html">Entities</a><a href="investigations.html">Investigations</a><a href="evidence-vault.html">Evidence</a><a href="search.html">Search</a></nav></section><!-- reader-governor:end --><main class="wrap section"><div class="eyebrow">Information Gathering</div><h1>SOURCE INTAKE.</h1><p class="lead">Submit a public-source lead, correction, missing record, counter-evidence, relationship note or page improvement. The rule is simple: sources become conclusions only after review.</p><section class="section"><h2>Before You Submit</h2><div class="intake-grid"><article class="intake-card"><h3>Source first</h3><p>Prefer official records, filings, public databases, archives, court/regulator documents, legislation, datasets or reliable reports with primary links.</p></article><article class="intake-card"><h3>Boundary required</h3><p>Every lead must say what the source shows and what it does not show. This prevents over-reading.</p></article><article class="intake-card"><h3>Leads are not claims</h3><p>Submissions are reviewed before they alter a page, score, card, clock, brief or conclusion.</p></article></div></section><section class="section"><h2>Submit A Lead</h2><form id="source-intake-form" class="grid" method="post" action="/submit-forum-post"><input type="hidden" name="board" value="main"/><input type="hidden" name="category" value="Source Intake"/><input type="hidden" name="title" value="Source Intake Lead"/><label>Submission type<br/><select name="submissionType" required><option value="source lead">Source lead</option><option value="correction">Correction</option><option value="counter-evidence">Counter-evidence</option><option value="missing record">Missing record</option><option value="relationship note">Relationship note</option><option value="broken page or link">Broken page / link</option><option value="daily brief update">Daily brief update</option><option value="risk clock update">Risk clock update</option><option value="card dossier update">Card dossier update</option></select></label><label>Evidence level<br/><select name="evidenceLevel" required><option value="1 lead">1 · Lead</option><option value="2 public mention">2 · Public mention</option><option value="3 primary source">3 · Primary source</option><option value="4 implementation record">4 · Implementation record</option><option value="5 convergence signal">5 · Convergence signal</option><option value="6 lock-in signal">6 · Lock-in signal</option></select></label><label>Source type<br/><select name="sourceType" required><option value="official page">Official page</option><option value="public filing">Public filing</option><option value="public database">Public database</option><option value="court or regulator document">Court / regulator document</option><option value="archive page">Archive page</option><option value="legislation or treaty">Legislation / treaty</option><option value="dataset">Dataset</option><option value="reliable report">Reliable report</option><option value="lead only">Lead only / needs verification</option></select></label><label>Source URL<br/><input name="sourceUrl" type="url" reader field="https://..."/></label><label>Lead title<br/><input name="leadTitle" type="text" maxlength="150" reader field="Short neutral title" required/></label><label>Date / year on source<br/><input name="sourceDate" type="text" maxlength="60" reader field="2026-07-08, 2025, unknown"/></label><label>Jurisdiction / institution<br/><input name="jurisdiction" type="text" maxlength="120" reader field="EU, WHO, ECB, US, France, company, court..."/></label><label>Affected page / card / clock<br/><input name="affectedRoute" type="text" maxlength="220" reader field="URL or page name"/></label><label style="grid-column:1/-1">What the source shows<br/><textarea name="shows" rows="4" maxlength="1200" required reader field="State exactly what the source supports."></textarea></label><label style="grid-column:1/-1">What the source does NOT show<br/><textarea name="doesNotShow" rows="3" maxlength="900" required reader field="State the boundary. What does this source not prove?"></textarea></label><label style="grid-column:1/-1">Missing record / next source needed<br/><textarea name="missingRecord" rows="3" maxlength="900" reader field="What would confirm, correct, strengthen or downgrade this lead?"></textarea></label><label style="grid-column:1/-1">Notes<br/><textarea name="note" rows="5" maxlength="1400" required reader field="Where should this connect? What should be reviewed next?"></textarea></label><label>Optional name<br/><input name="name" type="text" maxlength="80" reader field="Anonymous"/></label><label>Review request<br/><select name="reviewRequest"><option value="add as lead">Add as lead</option><option value="correct existing page">Correct existing page</option><option value="downgrade claim">Downgrade claim</option><option value="create missing record task">Create missing record task</option><option value="connect related pages">Connect related pages</option></select></label><div style="align-self:end"><button class="btn" type="submit">Submit Source Lead</button></div></form><p class="mini">No private personal data, threats, doxxing, spam, unsupported accusations, fabricated documents, or claims that go beyond the linked source.</p></section><section id="figure-source-status" class="section wrap source-status-panel"><h2>Figures & Sources</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card redline"><span class="label">Figures on this page</span><h3>Checked: 1 July 2026</h3><p>Numbers on this page are public-record leads. Crime, migration, sexual-offence, payout, death, and crisis figures must be tied to named official, court, police, parliamentary, regulator, or reputable source records before they are presented as settled.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Evidence standard</span><h3>What counts as a usable figure?</h3><p>Official statistics, court records, ministry releases, police datasets, parliamentary material, regulator data, or clearly named public reports. Nationality, foreign-born status, asylum status, immigration status, charge, suspect, conviction, and victim categories must not be mixed.</p></article><article class="card"><span class="label">Document trail</span><h3>Open the underlying record</h3><p>When the figure matters, follow the document link, source file, court record, official release, PDF, book, or video. The visible page should help readers reach the underlying evidence fast.</p></article></div></section><script type="application/json" id="compatibility-marker-vault" data-cleanup-marker="deep-cleanup">{"status":"compatibility-routes-preserved-with-clean-public-copy","checked":"2026-07-01","routes":["downloads/forum-posts.json","downloads/forum-posts.md","feed-center.html","share-center.html","launch-room.html","offer-center.html","source-document-vault.html","evidence-vault.html","black-file.html"]}</script></main><footer class="footer wrap"><p><strong>Review rule:</strong> a submitted lead is not a site conclusion until checked.</p></footer></div><script>const form=document.getElementById('source-intake-form');const hidden=document.createElement('input');hidden.type='hidden';hidden.name='body';form.appendChild(hidden);form.addEventListener('submit',e=>{if(!form.sourceUrl.value&&!form.note.value.trim()){e.preventDefault();alert('Add a source link or a clear note before submitting.');return}if(!form.shows.value.trim()||!form.doesNotShow.value.trim()){e.preventDefault();alert('Explain both what the source shows and what it does not show.');return}